            "adaptations.",
    },
]

const whyEyeson = [
    {
        id : 1,
        title : "Dedicated Creative Direction",
        description : "Your content follows a consistent creative direction instead of changing style with every\n" +
            "project.",
    },
    {
        id : 2,
        title : "Multi-Disciplinary Production",
        description : "Editing, motion, UI animation, design, storytelling, and sound can live under one\n" +
            "production relationship.",
    },
    {
        id : 3,
        title : "Brand Familiarity",
        description : "The longer we work together, the less time you spend explaining what looks and feels right.",
    },
    {
        id : 4,
        title : "Flexible Production",
        description : "Shift priorities as campaigns, launches, and business needs change.",
    },
    {
        id : 5,
        title : "Consistent Communication",
        description : "A structured workflow keeps projects, feedback, revisions, and upcoming work organized.",
    },
    {
        id : 6,
        title : "Built to Scale",
        description : "Increase production as your marketing operation grows instead of rebuilding your creative\n" +
            "pipeline.",
    },
]

const faqQuestions = [
    {
        id : 1,
        q : "What is an EyesOn monthly retainer?",
        a : "A monthly retainer is an ongoing creative partnership rather than a single project. You\n" +
            "reserve production capacity with our team each month, which can be used for agreed\n" +
            "types of content such as videos, ads, motion design, product content, social creatives, and\n" +
            "campaign assets.",
    },
    {
        id : 2,
        q : "Is the retainer only for video content?",
        a : "No. While video and motion are at the core of EyesOn, retainers can combine different\n" +
            "creative needs depending on your plan. This can include editing, motion graphics, UI\n" +
            "animation, product videos, short-form content, ad creatives, campaign adaptations, and\n" +
            "supporting visual assets.",
    },
    {
        id : 3,
        q : "How many pieces of content do I receive each month?",
        a : "It depends on your retainer level and the complexity of the work. Ten straightforward\n" +
            "social edits require very different production capacity from ten advanced motion-design\n" +
            "videos. Instead of promising an unrealistic fixed number of deliverables, we define the\n" +
            "expected production capacity and content mix before the retainer begins.",
    },
    {
        id : 4,
        q : "Can our content mix change every month?",
        a : "Yes. That flexibility is one of the main advantages of the retainer. For example, one month\n" +
            "might focus on short-form social content while another prioritizes ads, a feature launch,\n" +
            "and product videos. As long as the workload fits within your monthly production capacity,\n" +
            "priorities can be adjusted.",
    },
    {
        id : 5,
        q : "Can you help us decide what content to create?",
        a : "Yes. Depending on your retainer, we can help with concepts, hooks, scripts, references,\n" +
            "campaign ideas, content directions, and determining how larger pieces of content can be\n" +
            "repurposed across different platforms.",
    },
    {
        id : 6,
        q : "How quickly can you deliver content?",
        a : "Turnaround depends on complexity. Simple edits and adaptations can move significantly\n" +
            "faster than advanced motion design, product trailers, or complex UI animation. At the\n" +
            "beginning of each production cycle, we prioritize requests and establish realistic delivery\n" +
            "expectations.",
    },
    {
        id : 7,
        q : "How do revisions work?",
        a : "Feedback and revisions are built into the production workflow according to the scope of\n" +
            "your retainer. We use structured review stages so your team can comment on messaging,\n" +
            "pacing, visuals, animation, branding, and other relevant details without creating\n" +
            "unnecessary production delays.",
    },
    {
        id : 8,
        q : "Can you follow our existing brand guidelines?",
        a : "Absolutely. We can work within your existing visual identity, typography, colors, motion\n" +
            "language, tone, and brand guidelines. Over time, we also build familiarity with your\n" +
            "preferences so new content requires less explanation and becomes increasingly\n" +
            "consistent.",
    },
    {
        id : 9,
        q : "Can you create content for multiple platforms?",
        a : "Yes. We can produce and adapt content for Instagram, TikTok, LinkedIn, X, YouTube, Meta\n" +
            "Ads, websites, presentations, sales channels, and other digital platforms. Where needed,\n" +
            "one master creative can also be adapted into multiple aspect ratios, durations, hooks, or\n" +
            "versions.",
    },
    {
        id : 10,
        q : "Can we use the retainer for product launches?",
        a : "Yes. Retainers work particularly well for launches because one campaign often requires\n" +
            "multiple connected assets—such as a hero video, teaser content, social clips, feature\n" +
            "showcases, ads, and shorter campaign variations.",
    },
    {
        id : 11,
        q : "What happens if we need something outside our normal scope?",
        a : "Tell us what you need. If it fits within the team's capabilities and available monthly\n" +
            "capacity, we can often incorporate it into production. For significantly larger or\n" +
            "specialized projects, we'll scope it separately or recommend adjusting the monthly plan.",
    },
    {
        id : 12,
        q : "Is a monthly retainer better than hiring freelancers?",
        a : "It depends on your needs. For occasional isolated projects, a freelancer may be enough.\n" +
            "But when you need consistent content across multiple formats, managing several\n" +
            "independent freelancers creates coordination overhead and inconsistent output. A retainer\n" +
            "is designed for companies that value continuity, speed, consistency, and reliable\n" +
            "production capacity.",
    },
    {
        id : 13,
        q : "Is there a long-term contract?",
        a : "Retainer terms depend on the package and production requirements. We'll clearly define the\n" +
            "commitment, monthly capacity, scope, payment terms, and cancellation conditions before\n" +
            "the partnership begins—so both sides know exactly how the relationship works.",
    },
    {
        id : 14,
        q : "How do we get started?",
        a : "Tell us about your company, the type of content you currently produce, your channels,\n" +
            "expected monthly volume, and what you want to improve. We'll recommend the most\n" +
            "appropriate production setup and create a monthly plan around your needs.",
    },
]
---


<main class="relative w-full min-h-screen overflow-hidden">


    <HomeBackground />



    <VideoHeader

            BeforeHighlight=""
            Highlight="One Creative Partner."
            AfterHighlight={`A Month of Content.`}
            Description="Stop rebuilding your creative team for every new campaign.
EyesOn Studio works as your ongoing content production partner—creating a consistent
stream of premium videos, motion design, product content, ads, social creatives, and
branded visuals every month.
From one-off ideas to complete monthly campaigns, your team gets reliable creative
production without hiring and managing an entire in-house team."


            imageUrl="/retainers/1.webp"
            topText="MONTHLY CONTENT · CREATIVE RETAINERS · ONGOING PRODUCTION"

            primaryBtnText="Start Your Retainer"
            primaryBtnUrl="/contact"
            secondaryBtnText="Explore Our Work"
            secondaryBtnUrl="/portfolio"


            showBackground={true}
            backgroundClassName="
    bg-[linear-gradient(to_bottom,#010e17_0%,#01343a_35%,#34776c_65%,rgba(52,119,108,0.6)_80%,rgba(52,119,108,0.25)_90%,transparent_100%)]
    "


            headingClassName="text-3xl sm:text-3xl lg:text-4xl font-extrabold"
            highlightClassName="text-[#39d0c3]"

            textContainerClassName="space-y-5"


            primaryBtnWrapperClassName="bg-gradient-to-r from-[#0fe0d2] to-[#08717e] p-[2px] rounded-full"
            primaryBtnClassName="bg-gradient-to-r from-[#00A9BD] to-[#1D553A] text-white px-6 py-3"

            secondaryBtnWrapperClassName="bg-gradient-to-r from-[#08717e] to-[#40ae90] p-[2px] rounded-full"
            secondaryBtnClassName="bg-gradient-to-r from-[#00061D] to-[#0B1F2A] text-white px-6 py-3"


            imageWrapperClassName="rounded-3xl overflow-hidden w-100 md:w-120 scale-[1.2] lg:scale-[2.3]"
            client:idle
            />

    <LogoCaro tagline="Trusted by startups, SaaS teams, agencies, and product-led brands that produce content month after month." />

    <RetainersEditingSection client:visible/>

    <FeaturesSection features={features} badgeText="MORE THAN A VIDEO SUBSCRIPTION" title="Your External" highlight="Creative Production Team" description="Every retainer is built around what your company actually needs—not a fixed library of
generic deliverables."/>

    <RetainerCardsGrid
        beforeTitle="One Retainer."
        highlight="Different Types of Content."
        intro="Your content needs change throughout the month. Your creative partner should be able to
change with them. Depending on your plan and priorities, your monthly production can
include:"
        cards={contentPossibilities}
    client:visible/>

    <RetainerCardsGrid
        eyebrow="BUILT FOR CONSISTENCY"
        beforeTitle="Great Content Shouldn't Be"
        highlight="a One-Time Event."
        intro="The biggest advantage of a retainer isn't simply producing more content. It's building
momentum."
        cards={whyMonthly}
    client:visible/>

    <RetainerModelSteps client:visible/>

    <RetainerCardsGrid
        beforeTitle="From One Request"
        highlight="to an Entire Content Pipeline."
        cards={whatWeHandle}
    client:visible/>

    <RetainerCardsGrid
        eyebrow="ONE MODEL. DIFFERENT NEEDS."
        beforeTitle="Creative Support That"
        highlight="Scales With Your Business."
        cards={differentTeams}
    client:visible/>

    <RetainerContentSystem client:visible/>

    <RetainerHowItWorks client:visible/>

    <RetainerCardsGrid
        beforeTitle="Not Just More Content."
        highlight="The Right Content."
        intro="A strong monthly content strategy shouldn't produce twenty versions of the same thing.
Different stages of growth need different creative."
        cards={funnelContent}
    client:visible/>

    <RetainerCardsGrid
        eyebrow="YOUR TEAM, EXTENDED"
        beforeTitle="More Than Outsourcing."
        intro="The goal isn't to feel like you're sending tasks to an external freelancer. We want to
understand your brand well enough that creating together becomes easier every month."
        cards={whyEyeson}
    client:visible/>

    <RetainerPackagesSection client:visible/>

    <RetainerFlexibility client:visible/>

    <RetainerFinalCta client:visible/>

    <QandASection
        questions={faqQuestions}
        title1="Everything You Need to Know"
        title2="About Monthly Retainers"
        description="From deliverables and turnaround times to revisions, content types, and changing priorities, here's how an ongoing EyesOn partnership works."
    />

    <ContactUs client:visible />

</main>
